      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-409",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{1+1}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
