      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-410",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{-2}-{1}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980014/example-410.json",
          "file_sha256": "0cad8e2e275402e287cac3738acf8d615102b8ee697e19e2be01bcf9319ae7f1"
