          "question": "e-411",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\sqrt{64}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
